# Party banter while exploring Berez, Mount Baratok and the Tsolenka Pass. Each node opens with an `if` gate: the node
# is eligible only while its condition holds. Party members speak only through interjections.

~ banter_berez_nursemaid
if flag.berez_witch_met and not flag.lysaga_dead and not flag.lysaga_bargained
interject name:hedda_ironvow: A midwife. She brought him into the world. Somewhere back then there was a morning when he was only a baby, and she held him, and nobody knew.
interject tag:blunt: She knew. She said so. Teeth already.
interject name:hedda_ironvow: Mm. That's the part I'll be praying about tonight.
endif
-> END

~ banter_berez_marina
if flag.marina_truth_known and not flag.strahd_knows_marina_truth and not flag.lysaga_dead
interject name:tamsin_tealeaf: So we know something the lord of the valley doesn't. About his own nanny. That's the most valuable thing I've ever stolen, and I didn't even steal it.
interject name:silvain_aster: Knowledge you can't unknow is a poor kind of treasure. Who would we be telling, and what would he do with it?
interject name:tamsin_tealeaf: Something horrible to someone horrible. I'm trying to decide if that's a problem.
endif
-> END

~ banter_berez_told
if flag.strahd_knows_marina_truth
interject name:ilse_varga: We gave him a target and he took it. That's what you do with a weapon. You point it.
interject name:hedda_ironvow: We pointed the devil at a witch. I'll not pretend I'm sorry for her. I'll not pretend it was clean, either.
endif
-> END

~ banter_berez_ireena
if flag.ireena_saw_marina and guest:ireena
interject guest:ireena: Nine steps. I counted them before we got there. I don't remember learning to count them.
interject tag:cheerful: Maybe you're just good at stairs.
interject guest:ireena: Thank you. That's the kindest wrong thing anyone's said to me in a month.
endif
-> END

~ banter_baratok_mage
if flag.mordenkainen_met and not flag.mordenkainen_restored
interject name:silvain_aster: If that is who I think it is, the greatest living authority on half the spells I know is up a mountain arguing with a crow. I find that unbearable. Professionally.
interject tag:blunt: You find a lot of things unbearable professionally.
interject name:silvain_aster: It's a demanding profession.
endif
-> END

~ banter_baratok_restored
if flag.mordenkainen_restored and not guest:mordenkainen
interject name:hedda_ironvow: Did you see his face when it came back? Like a man waking up in a house that burned down while he slept.
interject tag:cheerful: He's going to be insufferable now, isn't he.
interject name:hedda_ironvow: Mm. Let him. He's earned a little insufferable.
endif
-> END

~ banter_mordenkainen_guest
if guest:mordenkainen
interject guest:mordenkainen: Stop looking at me as if I might wander off. I have my wits back. Most of them. The useful ones.
interject tag:curious: Which ones are missing?
interject guest:mordenkainen: If I knew that, they wouldn't be missing, would they?
endif
-> END

~ banter_tsolenka_watch
if flag.tsolenka_watch_met and not flag.tsolenka_gate_open
interject name:ilse_varga: Five men. A sergeant. Posts kept, roster current, mail oiled. Nobody came to relieve them, and they stayed.
interject name:ilse_varga: If Kestrel Company is somewhere in this valley, I hope to God it isn't like that.
interject name:hedda_ironvow: Then we look until we know, sergeant. Dawn comes.
endif
-> END

~ banter_tsolenka_gate
if flag.tsolenka_gate_open
interject tag:curious: "Nothing comes down." They kept that sign up for centuries. And we've just opened the gate.
interject class:wizard: We've opened it going up. Whether anything comes down is, technically, a separate question.
interject tag:blunt: Then we shut it behind us on the way back.
endif
-> END

~ banter_roc
if flag.roc_driven_off
interject name:tamsin_tealeaf: It had a sword in its nest. A whole sword. Somebody walked up here with a sword and became bird furniture.
interject tag:blunt: So walk faster on bridges.
endif
-> END
